web-monitor (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Age out channels after configurable audio/status inactivity (300 seconds
    by default); retain saved browser settings when streams return.
  * Reclaim idle catalogue entries and reuse channel objects still referenced
    by WebRTC tracks to support returning selected streams.

 -- Web monitor maintainers <web-monitor@localhost>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0800

web-monitor (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Receive radiod status beacons on each audio multicast group, port 5006.
  * Decode channel frequency, retain partial metadata updates, and expose
    numeric Hz values for browser display and sorting.
  * Keep status activity separate from audio activity and reject malformed TLVs.
  * Include channel-list sorting and corrected local-install interpreter defaults.

 -- Web monitor maintainers <web-monitor@localhost>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800

web-monitor (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Discover _opus._udp.local. services via mDNS and manage multicast
    memberships dynamically. Keep explicit groups and labels as overrides.
  * Enable discovery by default when no multicast groups are configured.

 -- Web monitor maintainers <web-monitor@localhost>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0700

web-monitor (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial local package with multicast Opus forwarding, WebRTC browser mixer,
    stereo pan, and a restricted systemd service.
  * Preserve the local /usr/local layout and /etc/radio/web-monitor.json.

 -- Web monitor maintainers <web-monitor@localhost>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:30:00 -0700
